                </font> 
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif">Also, ask 
                MSNBC's Ombudsman, Dan Fisher, if he still feels that Israeli 
                actions should not be called "terrorism", as he has 
                gone on record saying -- see: </font><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/cast/msnbcandterror.asp">http://www.pmwatch.org/pmw/cast/msnbcandterror.asp</a> 
                </font> 
              </p><p><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"> And also 
                ask the Washington Post's Ombudsman, Michael Getler, whose paper 
                has a long track recor of using "viglante" for Israeli terrorism 
                and "terrorism" for Palestinians, to comment on this. </font><font face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif"><a href="/sites/pmwatch.org/pmw/cast/vigilante.asp">http://www.pmwatch.org/pmw/cast/vigilante.asp</a> 
